Before we opened the café, another volunteer showed me the coffee machine.
It was my first time behind the counter.
I have never made coffee on a real espresso machine before.
"You have to learn to steam the milk," she said to me.
I looked closely at the many small buttons.
The machine looked very advanced.
She pressed the second button from the left.
The steam came out very quickly with a loud noise.
"Watch out, it is very hot," she said.
I kept a close eye on the whole machine.
I have seen the other volunteers use it.
I knew that I had to learn to steam the milk without spilling.
I did not want to make a mess on the clean table.
